xwriter, printpdf"},"276":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-23","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#stack","content":"Persistence"},"277":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-24","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#stack","content":"`tauri-plugin-sql` + SQLite (a single file in Tauri's `app_data_dir`)"},"278":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-25","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#stack","content":"Background API"},"279":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-26","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#stack","content":"axum on `127.0.0.1:22345` (default; auto-fallback if busy)"},"280":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-27","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#stack","content":"Async"},"281":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-28","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#stack","content":"tokio (`full`)"},"282":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-29","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#high-level-flow","content":"The desktop host (`apps/desktop`) is the only place that knows about Tauri. The four\n`crates/` are pure Rust and are reused by the standalone server (`apps/server`)."},"283":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-30","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#the-four-hard-rules","content":"Every PR must respect these. They are the load-bearing invariants of the system."},"284":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-31","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#rule-1--ipc-carries-path-strings-never-bytes","content":"Tauri commands take `pdf_path: String` / `image_path: String`, never image or PDF buffers.\nResult images are written to disk and the frontend loads them through the\n`asset://localhost/` protocol. This avoids the \"memory mirage\" where multi-hundred-MB scans\nwould be serialized across the IPC boundary. The `.shalgalt` reader/writer\n(`shalgalt-fileformat`) streams entries for the same reason — a project never lands in a\nsingle `Vec<u8>`."},"285":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-32","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#rule-2--no-ui-freeze-on-batch-work","content":"Long-running work (grading a stack of sheets) runs in a `tokio::spawn`ed task. Progress is\nreported by emitting `task-progress` events with snake\\_case stage names\n(`TaskProgress` / `TaskStage` in `shalgalt-core::domain::progress`). The command thread\nreturns immediately."},"286":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-33","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#rule-3--one-template-one-json-column","content":"`OmrTemplate` (markers + bubble groups + answer key) serializes as **a single JSON document**\ninto one `TEXT` column (`templates.json_schema`). It is never split into multiple columns or\ndenormalized. Coordinates are &#x2A;*normalized to `[0, 1]`** so a template works across DPIs and\npage sizes. The Rust struct (`shalgalt-core::domain::template`) and the TypeScript interface\n(`src/lib/types/`) are kept in sync by `ts-rs` codegen — never hand-edit the generated TS."},"287":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-34","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#rule-4--the-axum-router-never-owns-its-lifecycle","content":"The `Router` and CORS layer are built in `shalgalt-core::api`. That crate never calls\n`axum::serve`, never binds a port, and never reads environment variables. The host owns the\nlifecycle: `apps/desktop` wraps the router in a `tokio::spawn` + oneshot graceful-shutdown\nharness; `apps/server` runs it as the process's main task. Routes are versioned under\n`/v1/`; breaking changes require a version bump and an ADR."},"288":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-35","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#database-ownership","content":"All database access goes through `tauri-plugin-sql`. There is **no `sqlx` pool on the Rust\nside**. Migrations are defined in Rust (`apps/desktop/src/lib.rs`, SQL embedded via\n`include_str!`). The frontend reads and writes through `src/lib/db/*`. Rust commands never\ntouch the database: when a Rust task produces data that must be persisted (e.g. grading\nresults), it emits an event and the frontend writes it. The one exception is the standalone\nserver, which uses a separate read-mostly `rusqlite` `DataStore` in `shalgalt-store`\n(see ADR 0014)."},"289":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-36","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#see-also","content":"Workspace map — what each crate and app owns."},"290":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-37","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#see-also","content":"HTTP API reference — the `/v1/` surface."},"291":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-38","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#see-also","content":"The per-crate `AGENTS.md` files are authoritative for module-shape decisions."},"292":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","type":"page","content":"Build & run","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Developer"],"tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/build"},"293":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-0","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build","content":"System prerequisites and build/run commands for each OS."},"294":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-1","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#build--run","content":"Build & run"},"295":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-2","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#system-prerequisites","content":"System prerequisites"},"296":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-3","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#debian--ubuntu","content":"Debian / Ubuntu"},"297":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-4","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#macos-homebrew","content":"macOS (Homebrew)"},"298":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-5","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#windows","content":"Windows"},"299":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-6","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#pdfium-runtime-all-platforms","content":"pdfium (runtime, all platforms)"},"300":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-7","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#toolchains","content":"Toolchains"},"301":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-8","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#common-commands","content":"Common commands"},"302":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-9","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#first-run","content":"First run"},"303":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-10","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#running-the-standalone-http-server","content":"Running the standalone HTTP server"},"304":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-11","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#build--run","content":"shalgalt-omr depends on native libraries (OpenCV for the CV pipeline, pdfium at runtime,\nplus the platform webview toolkit for Tauri). Install the system prerequisites first, then\nthe JS and Rust toolchains."},"305":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-12","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#windows","content":"Per ADR 0001 the project uses the upstream OpenCV prebuilt self-extractor. LLVM\n(for opencv-rust's bindgen) ships with recent Visual Studio installs; otherwise install it\nfrom llvm.org."},"306":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-13","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#windows","content":"> Bumping OpenCV means updating three places: the snippet above, the `OPENCV_VERSION`\n> job-level env in `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, and ADR 0001."},"307":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-14","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#pdfium-runtime-all-platforms","content":"`pdfium-render` looks up the pdfium dynamic library at runtime. Download a release for your\nOS from bblanchon/pdfium-binaries and place\nit next to the executable, or extend `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` (Linux) / `DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH` (macOS)\n/ `PATH` (Windows). Release bundles ship pdfium as a bundled resource."},"308":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-15","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#toolchains","content":"**Node** ≥ 20 and **pnpm** (the repo pins versions via `package.json` / `pnpm-lock.yaml`)."},"309":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-16","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#toolchains","content":"**Rust** stable (`rustup`), with `cargo fmt` and `clippy` components."},"310":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-17","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#common-commands","content":"Command"},"311":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-18","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#common-commands","content":"Purpose"},"312":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-19","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#common-commands","content":"`pnpm install`"},"313":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-20","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#common-commands","content":"Install JS dependencies."},"314":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-21","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#common-commands","content":"`pnpm dev`"},"315":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-22","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#common-commands","content":"SvelteKit dev server only (browser, no Tauri webview)."},"316":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-23","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#common-commands","content":"`pnpm tauri dev`"},"317":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-24","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#common-commands","content":"Native window + Rust core (auto-runs Vite). The default flow."},"318":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-25","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#common-commands","content":"`pnpm check`"},"319":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-26","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#common-commands","content":"`svelte-kit sync` + `svelte-check`."},"320":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-27","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#common-commands","content":"`pnpm build`"},"321":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-28","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#common-commands","content":"Build SvelteKit assets (consumed by `tauri build`)."},"322":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-29","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#common-commands","content":"`pnpm tauri build`"},"323":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-30","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#common-commands","content":"Production native bundle."},"324":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-31","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#common-commands","content":"`pnpm generate-types`"},"325":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-32","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#common-commands","content":"Regenerate TS bindings from Rust (`cargo test -p shalgalt-core`)."},"326":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-33","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#common-commands","content":"Run these at the workspace root for the Rust side:"},"327":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-34","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#first-run","content":"On first launch the SQL plugin creates the SQLite file in the OS-specific data directory\n(e.g. Linux `~/.local/share/dev.filename.shalgalt-omr/`, macOS\n`~/Library/Application Support/dev.filename.shalgalt-omr/`) and applies migrations\nautomatically."},"328":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-35","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#running-the-standalone-http-server","content":"See the HTTP API reference for CLI flags, bind address, and auth behaviour."},"329":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","type":"page","content":"Contributing","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Developer"],"tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing"},"330":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-0","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","content":"Branching model, commit conventions, language rules, and the PR checklist."},"331":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-1","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#contributing","content":"Contributing"},"332":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-2","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#branching-model","content":"Branching model"},"333":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-3","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#commit-conventions","content":"Commit conventions"},"334":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-4","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#language-rules-mandatory","content":"Language rules (mandatory)"},"335":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-5","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#the-four-hard-rules","content":"The four hard rules"},"336":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-6","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#adrs","content":"ADRs"},"337":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-7","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#pr-checklist","content":"PR checklist"},"338":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-8","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#continuous-integration","content":"Continuous integration"},"339":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-9","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#branching-model","content":"**`stable`** — release branch. CI publishes from here. Never commit directly."},"340":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-10","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#branching-model","content":"**`develop`** — integration branch. Feature PRs land here."},"341":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-11","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#branching-model","content":"**`feat/<phase>-<topic>`** — work branches off `develop`. One feature per PR."},"342":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-12","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#branching-model","content":"`session/*` branches are local isolation only and must never be pushed to the remote."},"343":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-13","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#commit-conventions","content":"Conventional Commits, one short imperative subject line:"},"344":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-14","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#commit-conventions","content":"Types: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `docs`, `chore`, `test`, `perf`, `ci`."},"345":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-15","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#language-rules-mandatory","content":"Two languages, no overlap:"},"346":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-16","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#language-rules-mandatory","content":"**Code and documentation are English** — every comment, doc comment, identifier, log\nmessage, error string, commit message, PR description, and Markdown file in the repo."},"347":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-17","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#language-rules-mandatory","content":"**End-user UI text is Mongolian** (Cyrillic) — page titles, buttons, labels, validation\nand toast messages, help text. UI strings come from the single string table at\n`src/lib/i18n/`; components never hard-code copy."},"348":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-18","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#language-rules-mandatory","content":"`AppError.code` stays English (it is a stable identifier); the frontend maps the code to a\nMongolian message in the string table. A reviewer should treat any non-English string in\nsource or docs as a blocker, and any hard-coded user-facing string outside the i18n table\nas a blocker too."},"349":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-19","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#the-four-hard-rules","content":"A change is rejected if it violates any of the four architecture rules:\npath-strings-only IPC, no UI freeze on batch work, single-JSON template format, and the\nhost-owned axum lifecycle. When in doubt, read the relevant crate's `AGENTS.md`."},"350":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-20","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#adrs","content":"Architectural or operational decisions that are hard to reverse get an ADR under\n`docs/adr/` (`NNNN-kebab-title.md`, no gaps). Re-litigating a locked decision requires a new\nADR **plus** a master-plan update in the same PR. See the ADR index."},"351":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-21","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#pr-checklist","content":"Before requesting review:"},"352":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-22","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#pr-checklist","content":"`cargo fmt --all -- --check` is clean."},"353":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-23","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#pr-checklist","content":"`cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings` is clean."},"354":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-24","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#pr-checklist","content":"`cargo test --workspace` passes (unit + integration + ts-rs export)."},"355":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-25","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#pr-checklist","content":"`pnpm check` passes (no Rust↔TS type drift)."},"356":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-26","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#pr-checklist","content":"New behaviour has tests; coverage target is 80%+."},"357":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-27","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#pr-checklist","content":"No non-English strings in code/docs; no hard-coded UI copy outside the i18n table."},"358":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-28","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#pr-checklist","content":"No secrets committed; the axum server still binds `127.0.0.1` by default."},"359":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-29","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#pr-checklist","content":"Branch is rebased on `develop` and conflicts are resolved."},"360":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-30","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#continuous-integration","content":"CI runs on every push to `develop`/`stable` and on PRs targeting them:"},"361":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-31","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#continuous-integration","content":"Job"},"362":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-32","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#continuous-integration","content":"Purpose"},"363":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-33","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#continuous-integration","content":"`web-check`"},"364":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-34","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#continuous-integration","content":"`pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`, `svelte-kit sync`, `pnpm check`."},"365":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-35","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#continuous-integration","content":"`rust-check`"},"366":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-36","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#continuous-integration","content":"apt deps → `cargo fmt --check` → `clippy -D warnings` → `cargo check`."},"367":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-37","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#continuous-integration","content":"Both jobs must be green before merge. Release bundling (signed installers, pdfium download,\npackaging) and the updater manifest are handled by `release.yml` on `v*` tags. The\ndocumentation site is built and published to GitHub Pages by `docs.yml`."},"368":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","type":"page","content":"Overview","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Developer"],"tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev"},"369":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-0","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev","content":"Developer documentation for shalgalt-omr — a local-first OMR grading IDE."},"370":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-1","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev#shalgalt-omr--developer-documentation","content":"shalgalt-omr — Developer Documentation"},"371":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-2","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev#what-it-does","content":"What it does"},"372":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-3","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev#core-principles","content":"Core principles"},"373":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-4","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev#where-to-start","content":"Where to start"},"374":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-5","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev#shalgalt-omr--developer-documentation","content":"shalgalt-omr is a **local-first OMR (Optical Mark Recognition) grading IDE**: a Tauri 2\ndesktop application with a SvelteKit frontend and a Rust core that grades scanned OMR PDFs\nfully offline, persists results in SQLite, and exposes an optional background HTTP API for\nintegrations."},"375":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-6","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev#shalgalt-omr--developer-documentation","content":"This site has two audiences:"},"376":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-7","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev#shalgalt-omr--developer-documentation","content":"**Developer documentation** (this section, English) — architecture, the Cargo workspace\nmap, how to build and run on each OS, the contribution workflow, the ADR index, and the\nHTTP API reference."},"377":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-8","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev#shalgalt-omr--developer-documentation","content":"**Хэрэглэгчийн гарын авлага** (the *User* section, Mongolian) — installation and\nday-to-day use of the application."},"378":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-9","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev#what-it-does","content":"**Design** an OMR answer sheet in a visual editor (ArUco corner markers + bubble groups)."},"379":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-10","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev#what-it-does","content":"**Generate** a printable PDF of that sheet."},"380":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-11","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev#what-it-does","content":"**Grade** stacks of scanned/photographed sheets offline using an OpenCV pipeline\n(adaptive threshold, auto-deskew, per-bubble confidence scoring)."},"381":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-12","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev#what-it-does","content":"**Review** low-confidence sheets bubble-by-bubble."},"382":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-13","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev#what-it-does","content":"**Export** results to Excel, or share a whole project as an encrypted `.shalgalt` file."},"383":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-14","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev#core-principles","content":"**Offline-first.** No telemetry, no crash reporting, no analytics. Nothing leaves the\nmachine unless the user explicitly exports it. The optional HTTP API binds to\n`127.0.0.1` by default."},"384":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-15","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev#core-principles","content":"**Two languages, no overlap.** All **code and documentation are English**; all\n**end-user UI text is Mongolian** (Cyrillic). See the language conventions in the repo\n`AGENTS.md`."},"385":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-16","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev#core-principles","content":"**Stable contracts.** Four hard rules (IPC path-strings only, no UI freeze on batch work,\na single-JSON template format, an axum router that never owns its own lifecycle) are\nenforced on every PR."},"386":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-17","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev#where-to-start","content":"New to the codebase? Read Architecture then the\nWorkspace map."},"387":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-18","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev#where-to-start","content":"Trying to build it? Jump to Build & run."},"388":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-19","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev#where-to-start","content":"Contributing a change? See Contributing and Testing."},"389":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-20","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev#where-to-start","content":"Integrating over HTTP? See the HTTP API reference."},"390":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-21","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev#where-to-start","content":"> The authoritative sources remain the repository's `AGENTS.md` files (one per crate) and\n> the master plan at `.claude/PRPs/plans/shalgalt-omr-master.plan.md`. This site condenses\n> them; where they disagree, the code wins for behaviour and the per-package `AGENTS.md`\n> wins for module-shape decisions."},"391":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing","type":"page","content":"Testing","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Developer"],"tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/testing"},"392":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing-0","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/testing","content":"How the Rust and frontend test suites are organized and run."},"393":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing-1","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/testing#testing","content":"Testing"},"394":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing-2","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/testing#rust","content":"Rust"},"395":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing-3","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/testing#frontend","content":"Frontend"},"396":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing-4","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/testing#generated-artifacts-used-by-docs","content":"Generated artifacts used by docs"},"397":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing-5","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/testing#coverage-target","content":"Coverage target"},"398":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing-6","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/testing#rust","content":"Unit tests live in `#[cfg(test)]` modules next to the code; integration tests live in each\ncrate's `tests/` directory (one binary per file). Run everything from the workspace root:"},"399":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing-7","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/testing#rust","content":"Notable suites:"},"400":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing-8","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/testing#rust","content":"**`shalgalt-core`** — `template_serde` round-trips an `OmrTemplate` against a golden\nfixture (`tests/fixtures/template-v1.json`), catching accidental Rule 3 schema breakage.\nThe grading engine has unit coverage for scoring, partial answer keys, and confidence\nbanding. The `/v1/` router is exercised in-process over a `MemoryStore` without binding a\nsocket."},"401":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing-9","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/testing#rust","content":"**`shalgalt-fileformat`** — `roundtrip` (write → read, encrypted and plaintext, streamed\n1 MiB entry, deterministic order, manifest-has-no-PII), `bad_passphrase`, and\n`forward_compat` (a `format_version` newer than supported is refused before any\ndecryption)."},"402":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing-10","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/testing#rust","content":"**`shalgalt-cv`** — fixture-driven detection tests under `tests/fixtures/`."},"403":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing-11","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/testing#frontend","content":"Unit tests cover utilities, data transforms, and stores. Type generation drift (Rust struct\nvs generated TS) surfaces as a `pnpm check` failure."},"404":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing-12","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/testing#generated-artifacts-used-by-docs","content":"Two examples produce artifacts the documentation consumes — they are also a lightweight\nsmoke test that the public APIs still compile:"},"405":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing-13","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/testing#coverage-target","content":"The repo targets &#x2A;*80%+** coverage on business logic. Prefer fixing the implementation over\nweakening a test; only change a test when the test itself is wrong."},"406":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace","type":"page","content":"Workspace map","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Developer"],"tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace"},"407":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace-0","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace","content":"The Cargo workspace — what each app and crate owns."},"408":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace-1","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace#workspace-map","content":"Workspace map"},"409":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace-2","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace#crate-responsibilities","content":"Crate responsibilities"},"410":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace-3","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace#type-generation-ts-rs","content":"Type generation (ts-rs)"},"411":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace-4","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace#workspace-map","content":"The repository is a Cargo workspace with a SvelteKit frontend at the root. Rust code lives\nunder `apps/` (host binaries) and `crates/` (pure libraries). A single `Cargo.lock` and\n`target/` live at the workspace root."},"412":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace-5","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace#crate-responsibilities","content":"Crate / app"},"413":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace-6","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace#crate-responsibilities","content":"Owns"},"414":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace-7","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace#crate-responsibilities","content":"Must NOT contain"},"415":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace-8","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace#crate-responsibilities","content":"`shalgalt-core`"},"416":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace-9","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace#crate-responsibilities","content":"Domain types, grading, axum `Router`, `AppError`, xlsx, OpenAPI doc"},"417":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace-10","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace#crate-responsibilities","content":"`tauri`, OpenCV, pdfium, port binding, env reads, DB code"},"418":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace-11","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace#crate-responsibilities","content":"`shalgalt-cv`"},"419":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace-12","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace#crate-responsibilities","content":"pdfium rasterization + OpenCV detection + confidence scoring"},"420":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace-13","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace#crate-responsibilities","content":"Tauri, the axum router"},"421":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace-14","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace#crate-responsibilities","content":"`shalgalt-pdf`"},"422":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace-15","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace#crate-responsibilities","content":"printpdf rendering of a template to a printable sheet"},"423":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace-16","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace#crate-responsibilities","content":"Tauri, OpenCV"},"424":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace-17","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace#crate-responsibilities","content":"`shalgalt-fileformat`"},"425":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace-18","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace#crate-responsibilities","content":"Streaming `.shalgalt` read/write, age crypto wrapper"},"426":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace-19","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace#crate-responsibilities","content":"The `OmrTemplate` struct (lives in core), Tauri"},"427":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace-20","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace",