ns, axum spawn + shutdown harness"],[423,"Tauri, OpenCV"],[420,"Tauri, the axum router"],[265,"Technology"],[391,"Testing"],[393,"Testing"],[426,"The `OmrTemplate` struct (lives in core), Tauri"],[287,"The `Router` and CORS layer are built in `shalgalt-core::api`. That crate never calls\n`axum::serve`, never binds a port, and never reads environment variables. The host owns the\nlifecycle: `apps/desktop` wraps the router in a `tokio::spawn` + oneshot graceful-shutdown\nharness; `apps/server` runs it as the process's main task. Routes are versioned under\n`/v1/`; breaking changes require a version bump and an ADR."],[407,"The Cargo workspace — what each app and crate owns."],[282,"The desktop host (`apps/desktop`) is the only place that knows about Tauri. The four\n`crates/` are pure Rust and are reused by the standalone server (`apps/server`)."],[257,"The four hard rules"],[335,"The four hard rules"],[291,"The per-crate `AGENTS.md` files are authoritative for module-shape decisions."],[429,"The plugin-sql write path"],[405,"The repo targets &#x2A;*80%+** coverage on business logic. Prefer fixing the implementation over\nweakening a test; only change a test when the test itself is wrong."],[411,"The repository is a Cargo workspace with a SvelteKit frontend at the root. Rust code lives\nunder `apps/` (host binaries) and `crates/` (pure libraries). A single `Cargo.lock` and\n`target/` live at the workspace root."],[375,"This site has two audiences:"],[192,"Title"],[281,"tokio (`full`)"],[300,"Toolchains"],[387,"Trying to build it? Jump to Build & run."],[404,"Two examples produce artifacts the documentation consumes — they are also a lightweight\nsmoke test that the public APIs still compile:"],[345,"Two languages, no overlap:"],[410,"Type generation (ts-rs)"],[344,"Types: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `docs`, `chore`, `test`, `perf`, `ci`."],[268,"UI kit"],[518,"undo/redo харуул"],[403,"Unit tests cover utilities, data transforms, and stores. Type generation drift (Rust 