ive in `docs/adr/`."],[289,"All database access goes through `tauri-plugin-sql`. There is **no `sqlx` pool on the Rust\nside**. Migrations are defined in Rust (`apps/desktop/src/lib.rs`, SQL embedded via\n`include_str!`). The frontend reads and writes through `src/lib/db/*`. Rust commands never\ntouch the database: when a Rust task produces data that must be persisted (e.g. grading\nresults), it emits an event and the frontend writes it. The one exception is the standalone\nserver, which uses a separate read-mostly `rusqlite` `DataStore` in `shalgalt-store`\n(see ADR 0014)."],[238,"API port: default 22345, desktop auto-fallback, env override"],[367,"apt deps → `cargo fmt --check` → `clippy -D warnings` → `cargo check`."],[351,"Architectural or operational decisions that are hard to reverse get an ADR under\n`docs/adr/` (`NNNN-kebab-title.md`, no gaps). Re-litigating a locked decision requires a new\nADR **plus** a master-plan update in the same PR. See the ADR index."],[253,"Architecture"],[255,"Architecture"],[190,"Architecture Decision Records"],[189,"Architecture Decision Records — significant, hard-to-reverse choices."],[281,"Async"],[280,"axum on `127.0.0.1:22345` (default; auto-fallback if busy)"],[279,"Background API"],[352,"Before requesting review:"],[368,"Both jobs must be green before merge. Release bundling (signed installers, pdfium download,\npackaging) and the updater manifest are handled by `release.yml` on `v*` tags. The\ndocumentation site is built and published to GitHub Pages by `docs.yml`."],[360,"Branch is rebased on `develop` and conflicts are resolved."],[333,"Branching model"],[331,"Branching model, commit conventions, language rules, and the PR checklist."],[217,"Bubble label position: inside the circle"],[293,"Build & run"],[295,"Build & run"],[322,"Build SvelteKit assets (consumed by `tauri build`)."],[214,"Canvas wrapper + per-element layout modules in `shalgalt-pdf`"],[202,"Cargo workspace + crate boundaries"],[135,"Choose which **exam 