 written to disk and the frontend loads them through the\n`asset://localhost/` protocol. This avoids the \"memory mirage\" where multi-hundred-MB scans\nwould be serialized across the IPC boundary. The `.shalgalt` reader/writer\n(`shalgalt-fileformat`) streams entries for the same reason — a project never lands in a\nsingle `Vec<u8>`."],[432,"Tauri host: commands, migrations, axum spawn + shutdown harness"],[424,"Tauri, OpenCV"],[421,"Tauri, the axum router"],[266,"Technology"],[392,"Testing"],[394,"Testing"],[427,"The `OmrTemplate` struct (lives in core), Tauri"],[288,"The `Router` and CORS layer are built in `shalgalt-core::api`. That crate never calls\n`axum::serve`, never binds a port, and never reads environment variables. The host owns the\nlifecycle: `apps/desktop` wraps the router in a `tokio::spawn` + oneshot graceful-shutdown\nharness; `apps/server` runs it as the process's main task. Routes are versioned under\n`/v1/`; breaking changes require a version bump and an ADR."],[76,"The app needs **no internet** and sends **nothing** anywhere. Student data stays on your\ncomputer. See the Privacy statement."],[408,"The Cargo workspace — what each app and crate owns."],[283,"The desktop host (`apps/desktop`) is the only place that knows about Tauri. The four\n`crates/` are pure Rust and are reused by the standalone server (`apps/server`)."],[258,"The four hard rules"],[336,"The four hard rules"],[292,"The per-crate `AGENTS.md` files are authoritative for module-shape decisions."],[430,"The plugin-sql write path"],[406,"The repo targets &#x2A;*80%+** coverage on business logic. Prefer fixing the implementation over\nweakening a test; only change a test when the test itself is wrong."],[412,"The repository is a Cargo workspace with a SvelteKit frontend at the root. Rust code lives\nunder `apps/` (host binaries) and `crates/` (pure libraries). A single `Cargo.lock` and\n`target/` live at the workspace root."],[120,"This page walks you from **install → first templat